          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring (MR)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Treble (tr). UK term; US equivalent is double crochet (dc). Worked in clusters of 3."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Granny square (make 4)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "MR: ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, *3 tr, ch 2; repeat 3 more times. Sl st to top of ch 3. Pull tail to close ring. (4 clusters, 4 ch-2 corners)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: sl st to ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr in same sp (first corner). *Ch 1, [3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr] in next ch-2 sp; repeat from * twice. Ch 1, sl st to ch 3. (8 clusters, 4 corners, 4 ch-1 side spaces)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 3: sl st to ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr in same sp. *Ch 1, 3 tr in ch-1 sp, ch 1, [3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr] in ch-2 corner sp; repeat from * twice. Ch 1, 3 tr in last ch-1 sp, ch 1. Sl st to ch 3. (12 clusters)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 4: sl st to ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3, 2 tr, ch 2, 3 tr. *Ch 1, [3 tr in ch-1 sp, ch 1] twice, [3 tr, ch 2, 3 tr] in corner; repeat from * twice. Ch 1, [3 tr in ch-1 sp, ch 1] twice. Sl st to ch 3. Fasten off. (16 clusters)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Joining"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Block all 4 squares. Lay them in a 2 × 2 grid. Holding two squares RS together, work a slip stitch seam through both back loops of matching ch-1 side spaces along one edge, pulling gently to avoid puckering. Join the four squares in two pairs, then seam the two pairs together to form the placemat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Wet-block the assembled mat flat if needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Machine-wash on 30°C gentle cycle. Lay flat to dry."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
